{
  "_about": "Curated Google Fonts for wordmarks, grouped by voice. Every family here is free for commercial logo use (SIL OFL or Apache 2.0). `weirdness` is the lowest level on the weirdness dial (references/direction.md) where a group is in play; a group stays available at every level above it. `weights` are the ones worth trying for a wordmark; `text` lists calmer body faces that sit well beside the group; `note` is a rule for using the group. `small: false` marks a face whose detail clogs below about 24 px of word height: use it only where the wordmark is shown large, and keep a plainer lockup for small uses (craft.md, \"Decorative faces\"). specimen.mjs reads this file: --group <key>, or --weirdness <n> for every group up to that level.",
